## Interface: 30300
## Title: Encounter Journal (3.3.5)
## Notes: Adventure Guide for Wrath 3.3.5a — bosses, abilities, loot, and models for classic dungeons and raids.
## Author: ported from New Era (Ashgaroth) Encounter Journal
## Version: 0.1-port
## Dependencies: !!!ClassicAPI
## SavedVariables: EncounterJournalDB

# ===========================================================================
#  PORTING STATUS: opens in-client (micro button / slash / keybind) with WotLK
#  + classic data, loot and models. Remaining gaps are cosmetic (some chrome
#  atlases, model framing) — see README.md. Originally ported from Classic Era
#  (Interface 11508); the API gaps are bridged by !!!ClassicAPI + Core/Compat.lua.
#  In-code namespace is EJ (renamed from the New Era source's NE).
# ===========================================================================

# --- Gap-filler shims on top of !!!ClassicAPI (load first within this addon) ---
# Compat.lua also registers the UI-Frame-Metal-* chrome atlases ClassicAPI omits (was Atlas335.lua).
Core\Compat.lua

# --- Framework helpers (the EJ.* shared layer the journal calls into) ---
Core\Core.lua
# Skin.lua = UI skin selection (classic vs dragonflight); read by NavBar/chrome at build time.
Core\Skin.lua
Core\Modules.lua
Core\FrameUtil.lua
Core\PanelManager.lua
Core\TooltipWire.lua
Core\Texture.lua
# AtlasData.lua = the EJ_ATLAS coord table + Art\Common sheet registration for the modern chrome
# ClassicAPI lacks (DF tabs, RedButton close, MinimalScrollBar, inset trim, rock body).
Core\AtlasData.lua
# Tabs.lua = DF metal reskin for the journal's Dungeons/Raids bottom tabs (needs AtlasData).
Core\Tabs.lua
# NineSlice.lua = walker + the retail layout data (was NineSliceLayouts.lua); loads after Texture.lua.
Core\NineSlice.lua
Core\PanelChrome.lua
Core\Portrait.lua
# Dropdown.lua = classic UIDropDownMenu wrapper (replaced DropdownSkin.lua).
Core\Dropdown.lua
# Options.lua = Interface Options panel exposing the skin toggle (needs Dropdown + Skin).
Core\Options.lua
Core\ScrollbarReskin.lua
Core\NavBar.lua
Core\ItemButton.lua
# WorldMap.lua = the journal's "Show Map" button action (open the world map to the instance's
# uiMap). Replaced the non-functional WorldMap/{Dungeons,DungeonMap}.lua dungeon-overlay system.
Core\WorldMap.lua
# LFD.lua = the "Find Group" button action (open the 3.3.5 Dungeon Finder in Specific mode
# with the instance's dungeon ticked; runtime name-match against GetLFGDungeonInfo).
Core\LFD.lua

# --- Encounter Journal (original load order) ---
EncounterJournal\Assets.lua
EncounterJournal\Slices.lua
# Boss / loot / ability data — ONE consolidated file per expansion. vanilla creates
# EJ.ej.DATA; tbc + wotlk append (wotlk must load last, it replaces colliding Classic ids).
EncounterJournal\vanilla_data.lua
EncounterJournal\tbc_data.lua
# tbc_abilities.lua = OVERLAY of hand-seeded ability sections for the 8 Burning Crusade RAIDS (retail
# never authored journal sections for them), from DragonUI_NewEra's AbilitiesTBC.lua, keyed by the
# same DB2 encounter ids. Fills only section-less encounters; must load AFTER tbc_data.lua.
EncounterJournal\tbc_abilities.lua
EncounterJournal\wotlk_data.lua
# wotlk_abilities.lua = OVERLAY of hand-seeded ability sections for the WotLK RAID bosses the DB2
# extract has none for (Naxx/VoA/OS/EoE/ToC/Onyxia/ICC/RS/Algalon), re-keyed from DragonUI_NewEra's
# AbilitiesWotLK.lua. Fills only section-less encounters; must load AFTER wotlk_data.lua.
EncounterJournal\wotlk_abilities.lua
# loot_diff.lua = OVERLAY of difficulty masks the DB2 extract left undifferentiated (Ulduar 10/25,
# TBC dungeons Normal/Heroic), from NewEra's AtlasLoot tags. Loads after every *_data.lua.
EncounterJournal\loot_diff.lua
# item_info.lua = GENERATED itemID -> { name, quality, icon } for every loot item (AtlasLoot names +
# this client's Item/ItemDisplayInfo DBC icons), so rows render before the item is cached.
EncounterJournal\item_info.lua
# ModelPaths.lua = GENERATED displayID -> model file (+ scale, humanoid flag) from this client's
# CreatureDisplayInfo/CreatureModelData DBCs; the automatic SetModel fallback when SetDisplayInfo
# leaves the model pane empty (see EncounterPage.lua _PlayerModelFallback).
EncounterJournal\ModelPaths.lua
# npc_ids.lua = GENERATED encounter -> npc ids (TBC/WotLK, from the DBM boss mods) for the textured
# Model:SetCreature load path; Classic encounter ids are npc ids already.
EncounterJournal\npc_ids.lua
# worldmap_ids.lua = GENERATED 3.3.5 WorldMapArea id -> Map.dbc id for the instance maps (client DBC).
EncounterJournal\worldmap_ids.lua
# EJApi.lua = the RETAIL journal API (EJ_* globals, C_EncounterJournal, EncounterJournal_OpenJournal)
# re-created over EJ.ej.DATA for retail-era addon code (Details!, DetailsFramework, tooltip hooks).
EncounterJournal\EJApi.lua
EncounterJournal\ModelCam.lua
EncounterJournal\PortraitCam.lua
EncounterJournal\EncounterJournal.lua
EncounterJournal\EncounterPage.lua
# Search.lua = deep search (instances/bosses/abilities/loot) behind the navbar search box;
# must load before NavBar.lua only for readability — the wiring is runtime-guarded.
EncounterJournal\Search.lua
EncounterJournal\NavBar.lua

# --- Key bindings (registers TOGGLEENCOUNTERJOURNAL; labels live in Core/Core.lua) ---
Bindings.xml
